        "problem": "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}.$",
        "worked_solution": "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $\u2207f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
